data.content:
## What Changed: Microsoft.OpenApi v1 → v2

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets OpenAPI v3.1. Here are the breaking changes affecting your code:

---

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` removed

Schema `Example` is now a `JsonNode`:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;

param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

---

### 2. `OpenApiReference` / `ReferenceType` replaced with typed references

Instead of constructing a scheme + setting `Reference`, use `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference`:

```csharp
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
```

---

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a dictionary subclass

It's now a simple model with a `Schemes` dictionary:

```csharp
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new OpenApiSecurityRequirement
    {
        Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference, IList<string>>
        {
            [oAuthScheme] = scopes
        }
    }
};
```

---

### 4. `Nullable` property removed (OpenAPI 3.1 uses type arrays)

Nullability is expressed via `JsonSchemaType` flags:

```csharp
if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
{
    // Remove "null" from the type set instead of setting Nullable
    property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
}
```

---

### Fixed code (complete)

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

Remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;` — that namespace no longer exists.
